A1. Ask Mr. Nathan if he doesn't think this is a dumb show. ~ PANTOMIME
A9. This serves rolls and chops for breakfast, luncheon and dinner. ~ OCEAN
A10. Here is a sticker—if you handle it right you will find more than one point. ~ FORK
A12. Gandhi's laundry. ~ RAG
A15. We will leave it to you to work out this scheme. ~ DEVICE
A17. Don't get stuck with this kind of money. ~ PIN
A18. "It's a girl." Uncle Tom suggested this name. ~ EVA
A19. When a man does this he rues it because his home is sure to be broken up. ~ LETS
A21. The answer to the unemployment question. ~ NO
A22. This has always been a handicap to the shriners. ~ FEZ
A23. This is something that is overhanging Florida just now. ~ MOSS
A26. This plug can even stop the flow of traffic. ~ NAG
A28. This sounds like the "Puppy Blues." (By special permission of the puppy's right owners.) ~ WHINE
A30. This may give you some anxiety. ~ CARE
A31. A member of the Keeter family. ~ AMOS
A33. What the wheat crop might do to the market. ~ GLUT
A34. This started the Stein Song. ~ BEER
A37. As a matter of form a film star always breathes a little prayer before she does this. ~ EATS
A39. You will need permit for this. ~ LET
A40. He started to swear and this is as far as he got. ~ OH
A42. A Scotch measure. ~ DRAM
A44. No quibbling—this is just another form of lying. ~ LAIN
A46. Follow these directions and you may see South America. ~ SE
A47. An honest dealer always gets the right man to do this. ~ CUT
A49. India may gain her independence but she can never free herself from this. ~ ASIA
A51. If the wets want beer this is what they will have to do. ~ BREW
A53. Now don't say we didn't give you warning. ~ OMEN
A55. This is now permanently located on the coast of South America. ~ PERU
A57. This is what the Lindberghs always hear about themselves when they start on a trip. ~ ROAR
A59. These should be ruled by a firm hand. ~ LINES
A61. You will get nothing out of this. ~ NIL
A62. This puts it all over the Ford engine. ~ HOOD
A63. What some columnists do when they finish their columns. ~ ADD
A64. Putting it to a vote, this is what the eyes (ayes) have. ~ IT
A66. A member of the Brown family. ~ ANDY
A68. For no reason whatsoever this was pinched by an old crab. ~ TOE
A69. Since Japan has been making trouble in Manchuria, this is what the Chinese have under their hat. ~ CUE
A71. Where the Latin race started (plural). ~ ARENAS
A75. It does not take skill to do this. Anyone can do it. ~ ERR
A76. The end of the first lap. ~ KNEE
A78. An electrical terminal. ~ ANODE
A79. This fellow is so long-headed that he always snaps up a good thing when he sees it. ~ ALLIGATOR

D1. A pea-jacket. ~ POD
D2. The winner of the suit. ~ ACE
D3. The state people get into when they have marital troubles (abbr.). ~ NEV
D4. The suspenders our ancestors used to wear. ~ TAILS
D5. This is always starting tales. ~ ONCE
D6. Just supposing. ~ IF
D7. When this one gets soused only the wife knows how to handle it. ~ MOP
D8. The land of Ire. ~ ERIN
D11. What the farmers have to do to their onions. ~ KNOW
D12. A good thing to put in your note book. ~ REFILL
D13. The ways of the wicked city. ~ AVENUES
D14. This one always travels with a bunch of maps. ~ GAZETTEER
D16. They tell us this has started smoking again and is using a Sicilian ash tray. ~ ETNA
D20. The time the alarm goes off each day. ~ SAME
D23. Age makes this grand. ~ MA
D24. A good all round view point. ~ ORB
D25. Some of the big plants are dropping this in order to increase their production next year. ~ SEED
D27. A winning point. ~ GOAL
D29. This must be His Grace (abbr.). ~ HG
D30. When the electric ice-box came, Dinah used this for defrosting. ~ CHOCOLATE
D32. Don't blame this for your getting stuck. ~ STAB
D35. It will be a long time when you get this. ~ ERA
D36. Don't do this to your throat. "Consider your Adam's apple." ~ RASP
D38. A very unladylike way for a stenog to start a letter. ~ SIR
D41. This was a dampener for Henry George. ~ HUMIDOR
D43. This was put in just for the sake of appearance. ~ MIEN
D45. This man's performance was a hot one and a drawing act. ~ NERO
D48. This is not hard. ~ TENDER
D50. This will be on the air during the opera season. ~ ARIA
D52. What a man used to do to press his suit. ~ WOO
D54. A welcome wind in August but too abbreviated. ~ NE
D56. They found this safe in his arms. ~ ULNA
D58. The only thing that makes dishwashing attractive. ~ AD
D60. Operator! 0—0—8—1—2 Green. ~ SICK
D62. Did you ever see a man eating this? ~ HYENA
D65. This tin fish was found in the Atlantic and Pacific. ~ TUNA
D67. What time will do for the unemployed. ~ DRAG
D70. This has a very smooth skin and developed from Ponds (not an advertisement). ~ EEL
D72. The way Chicago school-teachers are being paid. ~ NOT
D73. What Lindbergh wishes to avoid. ~ ADO
D74. When Gandhi reaches India we hope he will have gained at least this much. ~ SER
D77. Those who ride in this usually look down on the Fords. ~ EL


